<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;"><p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Football has VAR, extra tim=
e and penalties. Apparently, it also has a subscription plan for delayed ju=
stice. Senegal=E2=80=99s fight to reclaim the Africa Cup of Nations title t=
hey won on the pitch =E2=80=93 only to lose it in the boardroom =E2=80=93 w=
ill have to wait a little longer, with the court of arbitration for sport (=
Cas) now targeting the end of November for its verdict. Yes, the final whis=
tle blew back in January. It is now October, and somehow, we are still wait=
ing to find out who actually won the thing. If you don=E2=80=99t remember: =
Senegal=E2=80=99s players walked off the pitch for 14 minutes after a late =
penalty was awarded against them. Several players even headed towards the d=
ressing room in protest before returning to finish the match. Morocco misse=
d the penalty, Senegal scored in extra time, and the Teranga Lions celebrat=
ed a famous victory. Two months later, Caf ruled that Senegal had forfeited=
 the match by walking off, overturned the result and handed Morocco a 3-0 v=
ictory. Senegal, unwilling to accept a championship decided after the final=
 whistle had long since become yesterday=E2=80=99s news, took the matter to=
 Cas. Their argument is straightforward: the referee allowed the match to r=
esume and finish, so why should the result be rewritten after the fact? Cas=
 had initially suggested a decision would arrive within days of the hearing=
 but the court now says its full ruling, complete with legal reasoning, is =
expected at the end of November 2026. In other words, forget extra time. Th=
is saga has entered extra months. So, for now, Senegal wait, Morocco wait, =
and African football fans wait =E2=80=93 while a tournament that ended in J=
anuary continues to enjoy an unusually long second half.</p></div></td></tr=
